\"answer\": \"Brazilian police arrested the treasurer of the ruling Workers' Party in connection with a bribery investigation at state-owned oil company Petrobras. The politician, Joao Vaccari Neto, faces charges of corruption and money laundering. He is the closest political figure to President Dilma Rousseff to be implicated in the investigation. Protests against the government, fueled by anger over the corruption scandal, have eroded Rousseff's approval rating but it remains uncertain how long they will continue.\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n"}
