mage of this lady halfheartedly scraping the fat glob honey mustard off of that sandwich. Like what is shrinkage at this location like? Anyways, I will definitely follow up with this. That glob of honey mustard tho....man...\\\"},{\\\"review_date\\\":\\\"2020-05-10 01:07:26\\\",\\\"review_stars\\\":1.0,\\\"review_text\\\":\\\"I made an order to take out paid with Apple Pay. I got to the subway to pick it up, two young male employees working. One did not have a mask and was constantly wiping his face. The other had a mask that sat below his nose. I asked the employee without the mask where his mask was, and he pointed to it sitting on the counter where the bread sits to make sandwiches.  DO NOT EAT HERE. I could not get refund, fed sandwich to crows during my walk home.\\\"},{\\\"review_date\\\":\\\"2018-10-22 23:25:41\\\",\\\"review_stars\\\":2.0,\\\"review_text\\\":\\\"Hardly any tuna in the sandwich. Tasted more of the bread than I actually did the tuna. Noticed that it is also being scooped up by a smaller scooper too. It use to be bigger. The guy that wrapped my sandwich must be new or something because he did not make the sandwich nicely (most ingrediants were on the wrapper and he also didn't wrap the sandwich correctly. Everything was falling out of it. I normally like all the Subway's I go to, but the one on Milpas needs to be less greedy when it comes to the serving amount of tuna, like I said before, there was hardly any tuna on the sandwich and also better at putting the sandwich together. I most likely won't go back to this Subway.\\\"}],\\\"state\\\":\\\"CA\\\"}\", \"answer\": \"Subway, located at 609 N Milpas St, Santa Barbara, CA, offers a range of options including sandwiches, fast food, breakfast and brunch. The store is open every day of the week, with slightly reduced hours on Sunday. Features include outdoor seating and takeout options, with no WiFi and no reservations required. The restaurant is suitable for groups. The business has received an 