can nominee in a district that has remained staunchly red in recent years.\\nAt DailyNewsNow we bring you the latest news from the West Coast and around the country, covering a wide range of topics from politics and campaign news to entertainment and local interest stories. Please feel free to share the story with friends and join the conversation in the comments below!\", \"answer\": \"Arizona Republican Blake Masters has announced his campaign for Congress in 2024. He will be running for Arizona's 8th Congressional District, which is being left open by fellow Republican Debbie Lesko. Masters, who lost in the 2022 race for U.S. Senate, stated that he wants to fight for Arizona's families and address issues such as inflation, border security, and water resources. He will face competition from fellow candidate Abe Hamadeh in the primary race, but the district is expected to remain Republican.\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n"}
