r and bright green. Stir or toss the broccoli constantly so all sides cook evenly without overcooking. Season with a touch of butter, salt, and pepper, and serve warm. \\n\\nFor steaming, fill a pot with 2 to 3 inches of water and set a steamer basket on top so that it sits above the water. Bring the water to a boil over high heat. Lay the baby broccoli in the steamer basket and place the lid on top. Steam the broccoli for 2 to 3 minutes, or until the stalks and florets brighten in color and become tender. Make sure to wash and trim the stalks before cooking. Serve warm.\"}"}], "temperature": 0, "top_p": 1, "seed": 70555, "max_tokens": 128, "cache_prompt": false, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}}
