, select a target for total cost of sales. For this example, we will use 35%. For every $100 in food sales, we would need to transfer $35 to COGS.irst, select a target for total cost of sales. For this example, we will use 35%. For every $100 in food sales, we would need to transfer $35 to COGS.\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"cost of sales example\\\"}\", \"answer\": \"Based on the given passages, it is clear that the cost of sales is an expense that a business charges against its sales to determine the gross profit earned. The cost of sales includes all costs incurred in creating the product or service that was sold, including direct labor, materials, and overhead. It is typically reported as a subtraction from net sales on the income statement and is calculated as the difference between the cost of goods sold and the beginning inventory plus the cost of goods sold.\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n", "add_special": true}
