nd lice\\\"}\", \"answer\": \"Based on the given passages, the difference between dandruff and lice is that dandruff is a condition of the scalp caused by the excessive shedding of dead skin cells, resulting in flaking and a slightly itchy scalp. On the other hand, lice are infectious parasites that infest the hair and scalp, causing an itchy scalp and occasionally an allergic reaction. Lice are small, brown parasites with six legs, while dandruff is a self-contained scalp condition.\"}"}], "temperature": 0, "top_p": 1, "seed": 70555, "max_tokens": 128, "cache_prompt": false, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}}
