 species, but this suggests we may need to take a closer look,\\\" Mate said. Fourth baby orca born this season.\\n\", \"answer\": \"A North Pacific gray whale named Varvara has set the record for the longest migration of a mammal, swimming 14,000 miles from Russia's Sakhalin Island to Baja, Mexico. Her journey surpassed the previous record held by a humpback whale and may indicate that some western gray whales are actually eastern grays, raising questions about the species' genetic diversity.\"}"}], "add_generation_prompt": true, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}}
