s usually in the upper left area of the screen. 2. This will prompt a 6-digit PIN. 3. On your phone, locate and select your \u201cSettings\u201d app, then select \u201cBluetooth\u201d, make sure the bluetooth is set to \u201cON\u201d.4.Under \u201cBluetooth\u201d select \u201cSync\u201d. Once your phone has been located, MyFord will ask if the PIN of the vehicle is the same on the phone. 5. Select \u201cYes\u201d on MyFord, and \u201cPair\u201d on your iPhone. 6.n your phone, locate and select your \u201cSettings\u201d app, then select \u201cBluetooth\u201d, make sure the bluetooth is set to \u201cON\u201d. 4. Under \u201cBluetooth\u201d select \u201cSync\u201d. Once your phone has been located, MyFord will ask if the PIN of the vehicle is the same on the phone. 5. Select \u201cYes\u201d on MyFord, and \u201cPair\u201d on your iPhone.\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"how to get iphone 6 to work with ford sync\\\"}\", \"answer\": \"To get an iPhone 6 to work with Ford Sync, follow these steps:\\n\\n1. In your vehicle, locate the \\\"Phone\\\" button, which is usually in the upper left area of the screen.\\n2. Press the \\\"Phone\\\" button and use the \\\"Seek\\\" or \\\"Tune\\\" knob to navigate to \\\"System Settings\\\".\\n3. Press \\\"OK\\\" to enter System Settings.\\n4. Navigate to \\\"Bluetooth Devices\\\" using the arrow buttons and press \\\"OK\\\".\\n5. Follow the prompts to pair your iPhone with the vehicle by entering the 6-digit PIN on both the phone and the vehicle's system.\\n6. Once paired, your iPhone 6 should be able to connect to your Ford Sync system.\"}"}], "temperature": 0, "top_p": 1, "seed": 70555, "max_tokens": 128, "cache_prompt": false, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}}
