 expected for the degree of fever) may occur in up to 50% of patients but is not a reliable diagnostic indicator. Faintly erythematous maculopapules or rose spots occur on the trunk and may become hemorrhagic.\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"what are the effects of typhoid fever\\\"}\", \"answer\": \"Based on the given passages, here are the effects of typhoid fever:\\n\\n1. High fever (up to 104 degrees F)\\n2. Weakness\\n3. Headache\\n4. Sore throat\\n5. Stomach pain\\n6. Diarrhea or constipation\\n7. Rash (on the trunk that typically resolves within 5 days)\\n8. Loss of appetite\\n9. Muscle aches\\n10. Severe headache\\n11. Confusion or agitation\\n\\nNote that typhoid fever can be fatal if left untreated, and it is important to seek emergency medical help if you experience any of the signs of an allergic reaction, such as hives, difficulty breathing, or swelling of the face, lips, tongue, or throat.\"}"}], "temperature": 0, "top_p": 1, "seed": 70555, "max_tokens": 128, "cache_prompt": false, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}}
