s than they die from aids, drug abuse, car accidents and homicide, combined. Cigarette smoking is a danger to our life and health.\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"cause and effect essay on smoking causes lung cancer\\\"}\", \"answer\": \"Based on the given passages, smoking is identified as the number one cause of lung cancer. According to Passage 1, smoking causes the majority of lung cancers, both in smokers and in people exposed to secondhand smoke. Passage 2 emphasizes that lung cancer is a disease that occurs when a primary cancer develops in the tissue of the lungs, and smoking is the leading cause of lung cancer. Passage 3 also highlights that smoking is responsible for the majority of lung cancer cases in the United Kingdom, with around 41,400 people being diagnosed each year. Additionally, it notes that smoking-related deaths are higher than those from AIDS, drug abuse, car accidents, and homicide combined. Therefore, it can be concluded that smoking is a significant risk factor for developing lung cancer.\"}"}], "temperature": 0, "top_p": 1, "seed": 70555, "max_tokens": 128, "cache_prompt": false, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}}
