racks and have a spring mounted on the door frame. If a roll-up door has only one torsion spring at the center, do not attempt to repair it due to the high tension; instead, call a professional repair service. For other types of doors, you may need to weigh the door and provide the drum information, door height, and track radius. This process can be done using winding bars and torsion springs if available, or following instructions for doors with extension springs. If the power to your garage is out with the door shut, pull the manual override cord, usually with a red handle, dangling down from the guide track.\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","generated":""}
