 then with all the possible food choices, she recommended the Beef Sliders, Mac Daddy (incredibly delicious), and Chicken Bites. \\\\n\\\\nStill so much on the menu to try, and looking forward to being there for their Happy Hour. Nice to have SB&K as an option for late night dining. Thanks again Hilary for taking such good care of us.\\\"},{\\\"review_date\\\":\\\"2021-11-19 02:53:52\\\",\\\"review_stars\\\":5.0,\\\"review_text\\\":\\\"Very cool place off the beaten path. Friendly staff, great food. Really nice outdoor patio in the back.\\\\nPlease get a larger mirror for the bathroom. ;)\\\"}],\\\"state\\\":\\\"CA\\\"}\", \"answer\": \"Seven Bar & Kitchen is a local business located at 224 Helena St, Santa Barbara, CA. It offers a variety of services and amenities, including lounges, art galleries, American (New) cuisine, bars, shopping, nightlife, restaurants, music venues, gastropubs, cocktail bars, and arts & entertainment. The business operates during specific hours, with opening times varying throughout the week. Notably, it is closed on Mondays, but opens in the late afternoon on Wednesdays, Thursdays, and Fridays. On weekends, it opens at 2:00 PM on Saturdays and Sundays. \\n\\nBased on customer reviews, the business has received mixed feedback. One customer mentioned experiencing unfriendly staff, an unclean bathroom, and incorrect drink orders. They were also disappointed to be asked to leave an hour before the posted closing time. However, another customer praised the establishment for its late-night dining options, vibrant atmosphere, and helpful server named Hilary. They enjoyed the outdoor patio and recommended the Westside Gin Cocktails, Beef Sliders, Mac Daddy, and Chicken Bites. Another customer appreciated the friendly staff, great food, and the inviting outdoor patio.\\n\\nOverall, Seven Bar & Kitchen has a rating of 4.0 stars. While there were some negative experiences, the positive review highlighted the potential for a enjoyable dining experience with good food and attentive service.\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","generated":""}
