7.35.350.185 D srv  log_server_r: request:  {"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Judge whether any answer claim is unsupported by the complete source. Return only JSON with p_hallucination (0 to 1), quote (one verbatim source string of at most 32 words, or null), byte_start and byte_end (half-open UTF-8 byte offsets, or null). A quote is evidence to inspect, not an entailment certificate. Do not use external knowledge. Input JSON follows:\n{\"source\": \"{\\\"address\\\":\\\"1111 E Cabrillo Blvd\\\",\\\"attributes\\\":{\\\"Ambience\\\":{\\\"casual\\\":false,\\\"classy\\\":true,\\\"divey\\\":false,\\\"hipster\\\":false,\\\"intimate\\\":false,\\\"romantic\\\":false,\\\"touristy\\\":false,\\\"trendy\\\":false,\\\"upscale\\\":false},\\\"BusinessParking\\\":{\\\"garage\\\":false,\\\"lot\\\":false,\\\"street\\\":true,\\\"valet\\\":true,\\\"validated\\\":false},\\\"Music\\\":null,\\\"OutdoorSeating\\\":false,\\\"RestaurantsGoodForGroups\\\":true,\\\"RestaurantsReservations\\\":true,\\\"RestaurantsTakeOut\\\":true,\\\"WiFi\\\":\\\"no\\\"},\\\"business_stars\\\":3.5,\\\"categories\\\":\\\"Breakfast & Brunch, American (New), Restaurants\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Santa Barbara\\\",\\\"hours\\\":{\\\"Friday\\\":\\\"6:30-22:0\\\",\\\"Monday\\\":\\\"6:30-22:0\\\",\\\"Saturday\\\":\\\"6:30-22:0\\\",\\\"Sunday\\\":\\\"6:30-22:0\\\",\\\"Thursday\\\":\\\"6:30-22:0\\\",\\\"Tuesday\\\":\\\"6:30-22:0\\\",\\\"Wednesday\\\":\\\"6:30-22:0\\\"},\\\"name\\\":\\\"Bistro 1111\\\",\\\"review_info\\\":[{\\\"review_date\\\":\\\"2016-01-30 13:04:56\\\",\\\"review_stars\\\":4.0,\\\"review_text\\\":\\\"We came here to eat and grab drinks while waiting for our hotel room to be ready.  This restaurant is located in the Hyatt hotel.  \\\\n\\\\nWe ordered Lamb meatballs, which was delicious and flavorful.  We also shared a Bistro burger, which contained bacon, cheese, mixed greens, tomato, onions and brioche bun.  The patty was juicy and tender.  \\\\n\\\\nI ordered a fruity cocktail, but I can't recall the name of it.  The cocktail  contained berries and it wasn't too strong, but had enough alcohol.  My other half got a mojito and said it was a great tasting cocktail.  \\\\n\\\\nOur server, Edgar was really attentive and gave us great recommendations.  \\\\n\\\\nAlso, if you check in on Yelp, you get 50% off an item when you purchase an entree.  \\\\n\\\\n*Parking- you can either park at the hotel for $25 a night and walk to this restaurant for find street parking*\\\\n\\\\nAlso, Happy Hour is from 4pm-7pm daily- small plates are $5, all beers are $4, all house wine are $5 and all well cocktails are $6 or Bartender's choice cocktail for $8.\\\"},{\\\"review_date\\\":\\\"2015-12-22 02:36:35\\\",\\\"review_stars\\\":2.0,\\\"review_text\\\":\\\"The waiter specifically suggested \\\\\\\"the salmon dish\\\\\\\".\\\\n\\\\nThe dish cooked too dry and was not fresh.\\\\n\\\\nThere are fish bones in the meat.\\\"},{\\\"review_date\\\":\\\"2015-11-11 22:51:42\\\",\\\"review_stars\\\":3.0,\\\"review_text\\\":\\\"So not sure if they the restaurant was under contruction or whatever but happy hour ended up being at the bar area by the pool. Which was fine with us. \\\\n\\\\nWe got the brussel sprouts which were really tasty. We got the wings which had a thick herb topping on it. The wings were crispy and good but the herb topping and sauce were kind of lacking. We also got a salad that I cant remember in detail but I remember there were apples in it. It was crisp and refreshing. The drinks were kind of weak which was disappointing.\\\"}],\\\"state\\\":\\\"CA\\\"}\", \"answer\": \"Sure! Here's an objective overview of Bistro 1111 based on the provided structured data:\\n\\nBistro 1111 is a breakfast and brunch spot located in the heart of Santa Barbara, California. With an overall rating of 3.5 stars out of 5, this restaurant offers a variety of dishes, including Lamb meatballs, Bistro burgers, and salads. The menu features both indoor and outdoor seating options, although the latter is not available.\\n\\nAccording to customer reviews, the service at Bistro 1111 is excellent, with attentive servers who provide great recommendations. One reviewer praised the restaurant's fruity cocktails, while another enjoyed their mojito. However, one customer was disappointed with the quality of the salmon dish, finding it overcooked and containing fish bones.\\n\\nThe restaurant offers Happy Hour specials from 4pm-7pm daily, with small plates priced at $5, all beers at $4, all house wines at $5, and all well cocktails at $6 or $8 for a bartender's choice cocktail. Parking is available at the hotel for $25 per night, or customers can find street parking nearby.\\n\\nOverall, Bistro 1111 appears to be a solid choice for breakfast and brunch in Santa Barbara, offering a range of dishes and drinks in a casual, classy atmosphere with friendly service.\"}"}], "add_generation_prompt": true, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}}
